Relationship b/w metamask wallets, infura, etherscan and blockchain
====================================================================

- We need a blockchain nodes to interact with the blockchain.
- Or, you need something like "infura", a blockchain nodes provider, who runs it for you and blockchain node is like the access to the data.
- The blockchain is the single source of the truth.

- "Infura" is one of the popular infrastructure providers to abstract running blockchain away.

- Data or smart contracts deployed in one blockchain is not accessible to other blockchain.


* How Metamask interacts with blockchain to fetch accounts/tokens/assets:
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- Metamask connects with "infura" behind the scene, an infrastructure provider which runs blockchain nodes in its data center and these nodes have convenient access of those blockchains.
And this way metamask talks with blockchain and has access of blockchain data.

Other examples: alchemy(infrastructure provider)

- In the context of MetaMask and Infura, Remote Procedure Call (RPC) is the "core communication protocol" that allows your MetaMask wallet (the client) to talk to a remote blockchain node (the server) run by a service provider like Infura.

- The standard protocol used by Ethereum and most EVM-compatible blockchains, and thus by MetaMask/Infura, is "JSON-RPC", which is NOT a REST interface, though they share some similarities and both often use HTTP for transport.

- In the blockchain world, the "procedure" is anything you want to do or check on the network:

